      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 8,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "closest_det_label, closest_det_bbox = closest_detection(detections)\n",
    "\n",
    "center = detection_center(closest_det_bbox)\n",
    "print(\"center[0]: \", center[0])\n",
    "print(\"center[1]: \", center[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "if closest_det_label is not None:\n",
    "    bbox = closest_det_bbox\n",
    "    cv2.rectangle(open_cv_image, (int(bbox[0]), int(bbox[1])), (int(bbox[2]), int(bbox[3])), \n",
    "                  (0, 255, 255), 5)\n",
    "\n",
    "arrayShow(open_cv_image)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If there are any COCO objects in the camera's field of view, they should now be stored in the ``detections`` variable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Display detections in text area\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll use the code below to print out the detected objects."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
       "model_id": "cdc103176e4d4b2bbd99fc29d93f6e60",
       "version_major": 2,
       "version_minor": 0
      },
      "text/plain": [
       "Textarea(value=\"OwlDecodeOutput(labels=tensor([1], device='cuda:0'), scores=tensor([0.1783], device='cuda:0', …"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from IPython.display import display\n",
    "import ipywidgets.widgets as widgets\n",
    "\n",
    "detections_widget = widgets.Textarea()\n",
    "\n",
    "detections_widget.value = str(detections)\n",
    "\n",
    "display(detections_widget)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "You should see the label, confidence, and bounding box of each object detected in each image.  There's only one image (our camera) in this example. \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "To print just the first object detected in the first image, we could call the following\n",
    "\n",
    "> This may throw an error if no objects are detected"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "tensor(1, device='cuda:0')\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "image_number = 0\n",
    "object_number = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "print((detections.labels)[image_number])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Control robot to follow central object\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we want our robot to follow an object of the specified class.  To do this we'll do the following\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  Detect objects matching the specified class\n",
    "2.  Select object closest to center of camera's field of vision, this is the 'target' object\n",
    "3.  Steer robot towards target object, otherwise wander\n",
    "4.  If we're blocked by an obstacle, turn left\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll also create some widgets that we'll use to control the target object label, the robot speed, and\n",
    "a \"turn gain\", that will control how fast the robot turns based off the distance between the target object\n",
    "and the center of the robot's field of view. \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "First, let's load our collision detection model.  The pre-trained model is stored in this directory as a convenience, but if you followed\n",
    "the collision avoidance example you may want to use that model if it's better tuned for your robot's environment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Great, now let's initialize our robot so we can control the motors."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from jetbot import Robot\n",
    "\n",
    "robot = Robot()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Finally, let's display all the control widgets and connect the network execution function to the camera updates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 54,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
       "model_id": "1291fc2449314978b8995f1139e685d3",
       "version_major": 2,
       "version_minor": 0
      },
      "text/plain": [
       "VBox(children=(HBox(children=(Image(value=b'', format='jpeg', height='300', width='300'),)), Text(value='[a ca…"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from jetbot import bgr8_to_jpeg\n",
    "from IPython.display import clear_output\n",
    "\n",
    "image_widget = widgets.Image(format='jpeg', width=300, height=300)\n",
    "prompt_widget = widgets.Text(value='[a can, a mug cup]', placeholder='Type something', description='detected object names', disabled=False)                          \n",
    "speed_widget = widgets.FloatSlider(value=0.1, min=0.0, max=0.5, description='speed')\n",
    "turn_gain_widget = widgets.FloatSlider(value=0.4, min=0.0, max=1.0, description='turn gain')\n",
    "\n",
    "display(widgets.VBox([\n",
    "    widgets.HBox([image_widget]),\n",
    "    prompt_widget,\n",
    "    speed_widget,\n",
    "    turn_gain_widget\n",
    "]))\n",
    "\n",
    "width = int(image_widget.width)\n",
    "height = int(image_widget.height)\n",
    "\n",
    "        \n",
    "def execute(change):\n",
    "    image = change['new']\n",
    "    image = image[:, :, :3]\n",
    "    image = cv2.flip(image, -1)\n",
    "    #print(\"image.shape: \", image.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "    prompt = prompt_widget.value\n",
    "    prompt = prompt.strip(\"][()\")\n",
    "    text = prompt.split(',')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    pil_image = Image.fromarray(np.uint8(image))\n",
    "    text_encodings = predictor.encode_text(text)\n",
    "    detections = predictor.predict(image=pil_image, text=text, text_encodings=text_encodings, threshold=threshold, pad_square=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "    num_detections = len(detections.labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "    for i in range(num_detections):\n",
    "        box = detections.boxes[i]\n",
    "        label_index = int(detections.labels[i])\n",
    "        box = [int(x) for x in box]\n",
    "        pt0 = (box[0], box[1])\n",
    "        pt1 = (box[2], box[3])\n",
    "        cv2.rectangle(image, pt0, pt1, colors[label_index], 4)\n",
    "\n",
    "    closest_det_label, closest_det_bbox = closest_detection(detections)\n",
    "    if closest_det_label is not None:\n",
    "        bbox = closest_det_bbox\n",
    "        cv2.rectangle(image, (int(bbox[0]), int(bbox[1])), (int(bbox[2]), int(bbox[3])), (0, 255, 255), 5)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # otherwise go forward if no target detected\n",
    "    if closest_det_label is None:\n",
    "        #robot.forward(float(speed_widget.value))\n",
    "        robot.set_motors(0.0, 0.0)\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "    # otherwise steer towards target\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        # move robot forward and steer proportional target's x-distance from center\n",
    "        center = detection_center(closest_det_bbox)\n",
    "\n",
    "        #print(\"speed_widget.value: \", speed_widget.value)\n",
    "        #print(\"center[0].detach().cpu().numpy(): \", center[0].detach().cpu().numpy())\n",
    "        \n",
    "        #print(\"speed_widget.value: \", speed_widget.value)\n",
    "\n",
    "        if center[0].detach().cpu().numpy() > 0:\n",
    "            robot.set_motors(0.1, 0.0)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            robot.set_motors(0.0, 0.1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        #left_motor_value = float(speed_widget.value + turn_gain_widget.value * center[0].detach().cpu().numpy() / float(width))\n",
    "        #right_motor_value = float(speed_widget.value + turn_gain_widget.value * center[0].detach().cpu().numpy() / float(height))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        #print(\"left_motor_value: \", left_motor_value)\n",
    "        #print(\"right_motor_value: \", right_motor_value)\n",
    "        #clear_output(wait=True)\n",
    "        #print(\"\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        #robot.set_motors(left_motor_value, right_motor_value)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # update image widget\n",
    "    image_widget.value = bgr8_to_jpeg(image)\n",
    "    \n",
    "execute({'new': camera.value})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Call the block below to connect the execute function to each camera frame update."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 55,
   "metadata": {
    "scrolled": true
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "camera.unobserve_all()\n",
    "camera.observe(execute, names='value')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "metadata": {
    "scrolled": true
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "robot.stop()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Awesome!  If the robot is not blocked you should see boxes drawn around the detected objects in blue.  The target object (which the robot follows) will be displayed in green.\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot should steer towards the target when it is detected.  If it is blocked by an object it will simply turn left.\n",
    "\n",
    "You can call the code block below to manually disconnect the processing from the camera and stop the robot."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 56,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "camera.unobserve_all()\n",
    "time.sleep(1.0)\n",
    "robot.stop()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Again, let's close the camera conneciton properly so that we can use the camera in other notebooks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "camera.stop()"
   ]
  }
